<figure class="r55-search" data-r55-search aria-labelledby="r55-search-title">
 <figcaption id="r55-search-title"><span>Figure 1</span> A match, an eligible row and a useful answer are different tests</figcaption>
 <p class="note">Teaching sequence from PostgreSQL 18.6 results · English · title A, description D · stock after order 103</p>
 <div class="stages"><div><strong>Parsed query</strong><p data-live data-query></p></div><div><strong>Lexical matches</strong><p data-live data-matches></p></div><div><strong>Eligible matches</strong><p data-live data-eligible></p></div></div>
 <p class="result" data-live data-result></p>
 <p class="explanation" data-live data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div class="controls"><fieldset><legend>Search text</legend><label><input type="radio" name="r55-query" value="mug" checked /> mug</label><label><input type="radio" name="r55-query" value="green_phrase" /> “green tea”</label><label><input type="radio" name="r55-query" value="minus_teapot" /> mug -teapot</label></fieldset><div class="buttons"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step aria-label="Step"></span></div><div data-hold class="hold" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>All three searches, as text</summary><p>mug matches P7 (rank 1.1) and P9 (rank 0.1). P7 has no stock, so only P9 remains; its description says a mug is not included. The quoted phrase green tea matches P3 (rank 1.1) and P7 (rank 0.1); only P3 remains in stock. mug -teapot excludes P9 lexically and leaves P7, which stock eligibility removes. It therefore returns no rows. Scores use ts_rank_cd with default weights and no length normalisation. The teaching stages distinguish decisions; they are not a trace of executor evaluation order.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 import observed from './native-observations.json';
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-r55-search]').forEach(root=>{
  const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw:n=>{
   const key=root.querySelector('input:checked').value;const q=observed[key];
   root.querySelector('[data-query]').textContent=n<1?'Not parsed yet':q.query;
   root.querySelector('[data-matches]').textContent=n<2?'Not tested yet':q.all_ranked.map(row=>row.split('\t')[0]).join(' · ')||'No matches';
   root.querySelector('[data-eligible]').textContent=n<3?'Not filtered yet':q.eligible.join(' · ')||'No eligible rows';
   const ranks=q.all_ranked.map(row=>row.split('\t')).filter(row=>q.eligible.includes(row[0]));
   root.querySelector('[data-result]').textContent=n<4?'Final result pending':ranks.length?ranks.map(row=>row[0]+' · rank '+row[1]).join(' | '):'Final result: no rows';
   root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=[
    'The same three products are searched. P3 has stock 10, P7 stock 0 and P9 stock 4. Text matching does not decide whether a product can be offered.',
    key==='green_phrase'?'Quotes become an ordered adjacent-lexeme query: green followed by tea. They do not request an exact case-sensitive byte substring.':key==='minus_teapot'?'The dash becomes lexical NOT: mug must be present and teapot absent. It excludes a document mentioning teapot, regardless of the sentence’s meaning.':'mug becomes one English lexeme. Both the Blue mug and the Teapot description contain it.',
    key==='green_phrase'?'P3 contains the phrase in its title and description. P7 contains it only in its description.':key==='minus_teapot'?'Only P7 matches both conditions. P9 contains mug but also teapot, so it fails the negative term.':'P7 names a mug. P9 says “A mug is not included.” Both satisfy the same lexical presence test.',
    q.eligible.length?'The stock predicate excludes P7 after order 103. The remaining text match is eligible; that still does not establish that it satisfies the shopper’s intention.':'The only lexical match is out of stock. No row satisfies both matching and eligibility. Limiting first and filtering afterwards would be a different query.',
    key==='mug'?'P9 is the sole returned row at rank 0.1. A successful indexed query can still give an unsuitable answer to someone who wants to buy a mug.':key==='green_phrase'?'P3 is returned at rank 1.1. Its title-weighted occurrence contributes more than a description-only occurrence under these chosen defaults.':'No eligible row remains. A useful interface should explain the active conditions instead of silently presenting an unrelated product.'
   ][n];
  }});
  root.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(input=>input.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render()));
 });
</script>
<style>
.r55-search{margin:2.5rem 0;font:.9rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.2rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:.8rem}figcaption>span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.6rem}.note{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.stages{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:.6rem}.stages>div{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);min-height:8rem}.stages p{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.result{min-height:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);font-weight:600;padding-bottom:.7rem}.explanation{min-height:8rem;padding-left:1rem;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent)}.controls{padding:1rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}fieldset{border:0;padding:0;margin:0 0 1rem;display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap}legend{margin-bottom:.5rem;font-size:.85rem}label{display:flex;gap:.3rem;align-items:center}.buttons{display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}button{font:inherit;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.45rem .65rem;border-radius:.25rem;cursor:pointer}button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.55}button:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}.hold{height:3px;margin-top:.6rem;background:var(--color-surface)}.hold span{display:block;height:100%;width:0;background:var(--color-accent)}details{margin-top:.8rem}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--color-accent)}@media(max-width:550px){.stages{grid-template-columns:1fr}.stages>div{min-height:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.6rem}.stages p{margin:0}.explanation{min-height:12rem}}
</style>
